# CODEOWNERS — Pablo
#
# This file gates review on the paths where a quiet change is hard to notice
# and expensive to get wrong: the agent rules, CI, the audit-logging surface,
# the schema, and the deploy surface. The intent is *not* to review every PR.
# Ordinary code merges once the required checks pass; a gate that fires on
# every change trains rubber-stamping and is worse than no gate.
#
# GitHub matches the LAST entry that matches a path. More-specific paths go
# below more-general ones.
#
# OWNER: @kurtn-pablo. The maintainer's day-to-day account and the project's
# automation both author pull requests, and GitHub will not let an author
# approve their own pull request, so the owner is a separate account that
# authors nothing. Landing a change below takes a deliberate switch to it.
# Never make an authoring account an owner here: it would deadlock its own
# pull requests on these paths.
#
# NO `*` FALLBACK, on purpose. With "Require review from Code Owners" on, a
# `*` entry would force a manual approval on every pull request, Dependabot's
# included, and nothing could merge on green.

